            <div xml:id="d239-a1">

                <pb facs="0483" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg427"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                        82.—Translation.]</seg><lb/><dateline rendition="#center">[From the South
                        Pacific Times, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1876-08-05">August 5,
                            1876</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Honorable Representatives</hi>: I have now to perform
                    my last duty as President by delivering to you the supreme authority of the
                    nation; and in doing so I have yet another to perform, and to thank the nation
                    for the assistance it has given me in the performance of a difficult task; to
                    thank you for the honorable proof you have given me of your confidence in me,
                    and all classes for their decided and friendly co-operation. I trust that these
                    common efforts may prove as beneficial to the republic as the motives have been
                    patriotic which have sustained us, and that when posterity gives its decision on
                    our conduct, it will concede that we have fulfilled our duty to our mother
                    country.</p>
            </div>
